From f1375f302bc929aafe2a41ad3aa1381efa0ae107 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "David C. Manuelda" <StormByte@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 07:40:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: enable VP9 high bit depth in the libvpx Meson port

vp9_highbitdepth=enabled reached Meson but was not in MESON_FEATURES, so
the config loop skipped it and vpx_config.h kept CONFIG_VP9_HIGHBITDEPTH
at 0. libvpx-vp9 then rejected yuv420p10le. Register the feature so the
header follows the option.
---
 meson.build | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 202e3743e..2e27fe042 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -343,6 +343,7 @@ MESON_FEATURES = [
 	'vp8_decoder',
 	'vp9_encoder',
 	'vp9_decoder',
+	'vp9_highbitdepth',
 	'postproc',
 	'vp9_postproc',
 	'multithread',
-- 
2.55.0

